    "type": "faq",
    "data": {
     "heading": "Property visa FAQ",
     "lead": "Real questions from property owners we work with every week.",
     "layout": "split",
     "items": [
      {
       "q": "What is the minimum property value for a Dubai investor visa?",
       "a": "There is no minimum value for sole owners — any completed residential property with a title deed in your sole name can qualify for the 2-year investor visa. Joint owners each need a registered share of at least AED 400,000. The 10-year Golden Visa route still requires AED 2 million."
      },
      {
       "q": "What is the difference between the 2-year property visa and the property Golden Visa?",
       "a": "The 2-year Taskeen visa works for any completed residential property (for sole owners) and renews every two years. The Golden Visa requires AED 2 million in property and gives 10-year self-sponsored residency with extra benefits, including no age cap when sponsoring unmarried children."
      },
      {
       "q": "Can I get a property visa on a mortgaged property?",
       "a": "Yes. For the Golden Visa the full property value counts even with an outstanding mortgage, and a bank NOC is no longer being requested. For the 2-year visa mortgaged properties are assessed case by case at the DLD."
      },
      {
       "q": "Does off-plan property qualify?",
       "a": "For the Golden Visa yes, where the DLD-assessed value is AED 2 million or more using the Oqood. For the 2-year visa the property must be completed with a title deed issued."
      },
      {
       "q": "How fast can a property Golden Visa be issued?",
       "a": "Our standard track is 5–7 working days. For high-net-worth investors in Dubai on a short trip, our VIP fast track completes the property Golden Visa within 24 hours, including pick-up and drop-off for the medical and biometrics."
      },
      {
       "q": "Can my spouse and I apply on a jointly owned property?",
       "a": "Yes. With an attested marriage certificate both spouses can apply — for the 2-year visa each spouse needs a registered share worth at least AED 400,000."
      },
      {
       "q": "Can I sponsor my family on a property visa?",
       "a": "Yes — both the 2-year visa and the property Golden Visa allow you to sponsor your spouse and children, and parents. We process the dependants' permits, medicals and Emirates IDs in the same file."
      },
      {
       "q": "Can I work on a property investor visa?",
       "a": "The visa gives you residency but not an automatic right to salaried employment — that still needs a work permit through the employer. You can run your own business under your licence."
      }
     ],
     "theme": "light"
    }
