      {
       "heading": "How the ICP process works",
       "body": "Whether it is a first card or a renewal, ICP runs the same five stages — we handle every one of them online.",
       "points": "Application (typing) — we prepare and submit the ICP eForm, usually within the hour\nPayment — card fee AED 200 / 300 / 600 / 1,100 by validity plus AED 85 application and typing\nBiometrics — fingerprints at an ICP centre for first-time applicants; we book the slot\nPrinting — the card is printed typically 24–48 hours after approval\nDelivery — collect from your chosen Emirates Post office or track it in the ICP app"
      },
      {
       "heading": "Documents required",
       "body": "The exact list depends on whether it is a new card, a renewal or a replacement.",
       "points": "Original passport and copy\nResidence visa or entry permit copy\nPersonal photo with a white background\nSponsor documents for dependants\nAttested birth certificate for newborns and children\nPolice report for a lost card replacement"
      },
      {
       "heading": "Government fees at a glance (2026)",
       "body": "The card fee depends on the validity of your residence visa; the application and typing fee is a flat AED 85.",
       "points": "New card, 1 year — AED 200 card fee + AED 85 application and typing = AED 285\nNew card, 2 years — AED 300 + AED 85 = AED 385\nNew card, 5 years (Golden Visa) — AED 600 + AED 85 = AED 685\nNew card, 10 years (Golden Visa) — AED 1,100 + AED 85 = AED 1,185\nRenewal, 2 years — AED 300 + AED 85 = AED 385\nLost or damaged replacement — AED 400 + AED 85 = AED 485\nUrgent Fawri service — additional AED 150 for 24-hour issuance\nLate renewal fine — AED 20 per day after the 30-day grace period, capped at AED 1,000"
      },
      {
       "heading": "What we handle for you",
       "body": "The same service a typing centre offers, minus the drive, the queue and the guesswork.",
       "points": "Typing and filing of the ICP application with your documents attached\nBiometric appointment booking at the nearest ICP centre\nUrgent Fawri handling where the case is eligible\nApplication follow-up with ICP until the card is in your hand\nWhole-family processing — spouse, children, newborns, parents and domestic staff\nUpfront itemised cost: government fee versus service charge, in writing"
      }
