  "excerpt": "Category thresholds, new professional routes and the documentation authorities now expect at nomination stage.",
  "content": "<p>The Golden Visa framework has widened again, and the practical effect is that profiles previously refused now qualify under a different category rather than a different threshold.</p><p>The most significant movement is in specialised talent. Nomination letters from recognised UAE institutions carry more weight than salary evidence alone, and applicants who present both are approved noticeably faster.</p><p>For property investors, the AED 2 million threshold remains, but aggregation across multiple deeds is now routinely accepted where ownership is clearly evidenced.</p><p>Our advice remains unchanged: choose the category where your evidence is strongest, not the one that sounds most prestigious.</p>",
